.Dd August 2, 2026
.Dt MORB 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm morb
.Nd control the Morbstack VM and the containers running inside it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Op Fl -help | Fl h
.Nm
.Cm status | start | stop | suspend | resume | shares | version | doctor
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm stop | reset-disk
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm rosetta
.Op Cm status | install
.Op Fl -print-plan
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm k8s
.Op Cm status | enable | disable
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm k8s Cm kubeconfig
.Op Fl -merge
.Op Fl -switch-context
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line client for
.Sy morbstackd ,
the Morbstack daemon
.Pq no separate man page ships for it yet
that runs a single Linux virtual machine on macOS via
.Em Virtualization.framework
and forwards the Docker Engine API out of it.
Most subcommands talk to
.Nm morbstackd
over a local Unix-domain socket; a few
.Pq Cm shares , Cm rosetta status , Cm doctor
answer from host-side state alone and never require the daemon to be
running.
.Pp
Commands that need the VM running
.Po
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
.Cm suspend ,
.Cm resume ,
.Cm k8s enable ,
.Cm k8s disable ,
.Cm k8s kubeconfig
.Pc
will start
.Nm morbstackd
on demand if it is not already running and a sibling
.Nm morbstackd
binary can be found and is correctly signed for virtualization.
Purely observational commands
.Po
.Cm status ,
.Cm shares ,
.Cm rosetta status ,
.Cm doctor
.Pc
never do this: if the daemon is not running they report that fact instead
of starting one just to ask it a question.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Show daemon and VM state: lifecycle state, guest control channel, Docker
readiness, where container data is stored, active connections, published
ports, and daemon version.
.It Cm start
Boot the VM.
.It Cm stop
Shut the VM down.
Accepts
.Fl -force
to stop without first asking the guest to shut down cleanly.
.It Cm suspend
Save the VM to disk and free the memory and CPU it was using.
On a host where save/restore is unsupported this behaves like
.Cm stop
and the containers do not survive it; the daemon reports this via a note
in the response.
.It Cm resume
Restore a VM previously put down with
.Cm suspend .
.It Cm shares
List the shared host paths configured in
.Pa config.toml
and, if the daemon is running, whether the guest actually has each one
mounted.
Answerable without the daemon.
.It Cm rosetta Op Cm status
Show whether Rosetta is installed on the host, enabled in the Morbstack
config, and active in the guest.
This is the default when
.Cm rosetta
is given no subcommand.
Answerable without the daemon.
.It Cm rosetta Cm install
Install Rosetta for Linux and enable it in the Morbstack config.
Always prompts for interactive confirmation on a terminal before doing
anything; refuses to run with stdin not a terminal.
Installing Rosetta itself triggers a separate, unavoidable macOS system
licence prompt that
.Nm
does not and cannot answer on the user's behalf.
Accepts
.Fl -print-plan
to print exactly what it would do and exit without doing it.
Does
.Em not
accept
.Fl -force :
this is deliberate, and passing it is a hard error.
See
.Sx OPTIONS .
.It Cm k8s Op Cm status
Show whether the local Kubernetes cluster is installed in the guest,
enabled, and how many nodes/pods are Ready.
This is the default when
.Cm k8s
is given no subcommand.
.It Cm k8s Cm enable
Install the Kubernetes payload into the guest if it is not already
there, then start the cluster.
May start the daemon and the VM.
.It Cm k8s Cm disable
Stop the cluster.
The installed payload and its on-disk state are left in place.
.It Cm k8s Cm kubeconfig
Write a kubeconfig for the Morbstack cluster to
.Pa ~/.morbstack/kubeconfig .
With
.Fl -merge ,
instead merge a
.Dq morbstack
cluster/user/context into
.Pa ~/.kube/config ,
after asking for confirmation and writing a timestamped backup of that
file first; add
.Fl -switch-context
to also point
.Cm current-context
at
.Dq morbstack
as part of the merge.
.Fl -force
skips the merge confirmation prompt.
.It Cm version
Print the CLI version, and the daemon's version if it can be reached.
Never fails just because nothing is running.
.It Cm doctor
Diagnose the host: signature/entitlement checks, kernel/initrd presence,
Rosetta support, and similar preflight facts.
Works without the daemon.
Exits 2 if any check is unhealthy.
.It Cm reset-disk
Delete the Docker data disk image
.Pq Pa ~/.morbstack/data/disk.img
and nothing else under
.Pa ~/.morbstack ,
so every image, container and volume in the VM is gone on the next
.Cm start .
Refuses to run while the VM is in any state other than
.Dq stopped
or
.Dq error .
Prompts for interactive confirmation unless
.Fl -force
is given.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Emit raw JSON instead of human-readable output.
Recognized anywhere on the command line, not only after the command; it
is stripped from the argument list before the command itself is even
read, so
.Nm morb --json status
and
.Nm morb status --json
are identical.
.It Fl -force
Skip a confirmation prompt.
Its meaning depends on the command: for
.Cm stop
it skips asking the guest to shut down cleanly first; for
.Cm reset-disk
and
.Cm k8s kubeconfig --merge
it skips the interactive
.Dq are you sure
prompt.
It is silently ignored (not rejected) on every other command, including
.Cm start , suspend , resume , k8s status , k8s enable
and
.Cm k8s disable ,
where it is never read by the parser at all.
It is deliberately
.Em refused
.Pq a hard error, exit 2
by
.Cm rosetta install ,
which installs system software under Apple's licence and therefore
always asks the person at the keyboard regardless of any flag; use
.Fl -print-plan
to preview it, or run
.Xr softwareupdate 8
.Fl -install-rosetta
directly for an unattended install.
.It Fl -print-plan
Valid only for
.Cm rosetta install .
Prints the exact steps that command would take and exits without taking
them.
.It Fl -merge
Valid only for
.Cm k8s kubeconfig .
Merge the Morbstack context into
.Pa ~/.kube/config
instead of only writing the standalone kubeconfig file.
.It Fl -switch-context
Valid only for
.Cm k8s kubeconfig
alongside
.Fl -merge .
Also switch
.Cm current-context
to
.Dq morbstack
as part of the merge.
This flag exists and is honored by
.Nm ,
but is not mentioned anywhere in
.Nm morb --help Ns 's
own usage text.
.It Fl -help , Fl h
Print the top-level usage summary and exit 0.
Recognized anywhere on the command line and checked before any
subcommand is parsed, so it always prints the same global summary rather
than help for the specific subcommand it follows;
.Nm morb k8s kubeconfig --help
prints the same text as
.Nm morb --help .
.Fl h
works identically to
.Fl -help
but is not listed in
.Nm morb --help Ns 's
own OPTIONS section.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Nm Ns 's
argument parser and command dispatch
.Pq mac/Sources/morb/main.swift
do not read any environment variables; every path it uses comes from a
fixed, compiled-in location under
.Pa ~/.morbstack .
No
.Ev MORBSTACK_HOME
or equivalent override is consulted at that layer.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.morbstack/run/morbstackd.sock"
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/run/docker.sock
Unix-domain socket that relays the Docker Engine API out of the guest.
Point
.Ev DOCKER_HOST
at it, e.g.
.Dl DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.morbstack/run/docker.sock docker ps
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/run/morbstackd.sock
Unix-domain control socket
.Nm
uses to talk to
.Nm morbstackd
(newline-delimited JSON).
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/kubeconfig
Kubeconfig written by
.Cm k8s kubeconfig .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/data/disk.img
The Docker data disk image; deleted by
.Cm reset-disk .
.It Pa ~/.morbstack/config.toml
Host-side configuration, including
.Cm shared_paths
and the
.Cm rosetta
setting toggled by
.Cm rosetta install .
.It Pa ~/.kube/config
The user's own kubectl config, edited only by
.Cm k8s kubeconfig --merge ,
and only after asking and taking a timestamped backup.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
.Nm morbstackd
could not be reached: it was not running, no sibling
.Nm morbstackd
binary was found or it was not signed for virtualization, or it could
not be started or bound its socket in time.
.It 2
The command ran but failed: an unknown command or subcommand, a rejected
flag combination
.Pq e.g. Cm rosetta install Fl -force ,
a cancelled confirmation prompt, a check that
.Cm doctor
reports unhealthy, or a daemon-reported failure.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Boot the VM and check on it
.Dl morb start
.Dl morb status
.It Run a container through the relayed Docker socket
.Dl DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.morbstack/run/docker.sock docker run --rm hello-world
.It Preview a Rosetta install without doing it
.Dl morb rosetta install --print-plan
.It Bring up the local Kubernetes cluster and use it
.Dl morb k8s enable
.Dl morb k8s kubeconfig --merge --switch-context
.Dl kubectl get nodes
.It Get machine-readable status for scripting
.Dl morb status --json
.It Start over with an empty Docker data disk
.Dl morb stop
.Dl morb reset-disk --force
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr docker 1 ,
.Xr docker-compose 1 ,
.Xr kubectl 1 ,
.Xr softwareupdate 8
